Well, how about using goi for always reassignment, and no'u for the
alternative.

ko'a goi la fred. li'o .i ko'a goi la djan.
A is Fred. ... Now A is John. (Fred is not John, A has new meaning.)


ko'a goi la fred. li'o .i ko'a no'uji'a la djan.
A is Fred. ... A also is John, lo, John is Fred!

Since no'u doesn't reassign ko'a, but explains it, this is equal to
offering a new fact about ko'a as it exists.



